{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122334","id":4262223512,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7-DF6Y","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122334","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122334.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122334.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122334","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122334/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122334/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122334/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6356dd2be003998b357d6e2241daee5638365f43","number":122334,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix signal connect dialog crashes.","user":{"login":"saierXP","id":45038185,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDM4MTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45038185?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP","html_url":"https://github.com/saierXP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #121630 \r\n- Closes #116235\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n\r\n#101145 fixed signal connection crash, and #113789 introduced regression.\r\n\r\nWhen the signal connection is initialized, because it is not yet visible, the cache after scene changes is not cleared during the `_update_tree`, which may lead to access to freed nodes.\r\n\r\nThe process of reproduction is as follows: \r\nOpen two scenes, A and B. Trigger two connections in scene B. After the tooltip pops up, close scene B using `Ctrl + W`. \r\nConnecting in scene A will have a high probability of triggering a crash. If no crash occurs, close scenes A and B and try again.\r\n`Ctrl + W` is a custom keyboard shortcut for `ui_close_dialog` and `close_scene`.\r\n\r\nI don't know why it requires two connection and tooltips, which causes the cache to not be cleared.\r\n\r\n[connect.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e90e669f-9f3c-4e97-b0d7-94f839031b78)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:edit